m("'One has to convey in a language that is not one's own the spirit that is one's own.' This is from:",["Rushdie's 'Imaginary Homelands'","Raja Rao's Foreword to 'Kanthapura'","Kamala Das's 'An Introduction'","Tagore's 'Nationalism'"],1,"Raja Rao, Foreword to Kanthapura (1938)."),
m("Assertion (A): Indian English is syllable-timed. Reason (R): Indian languages generally give syllables roughly equal duration.",["Both A and R true; R explains A","Both true; R does not explain A","A true, R false","A false, R true"],0,"The syllable-timed rhythm of Indian English is attributed to L1 transfer."),
